{"resource":{"id":"rust-answer-key","title":"Rust — Answer Key","category":"Programming","difficulty":"Beginner","readingTime":"26 min","pages":32,"lastUpdated":"April 2026","tags":["Programming","Rust","Systems"],"heroImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1461749280684-dccba630e2f6?w=1800&q=80","heroSubtitle":"Fully-explained solutions to the Rust Practice Questions workbook — reasoning, alternatives, optimization tips, and rubrics."},"toc":[{"id":"objectives","label":"Learning Objectives"},{"id":"s1","label":"1. MCQ Answers"},{"id":"s2","label":"2. Output Prediction"},{"id":"s3","label":"3. Ownership Puzzles"},{"id":"s4","label":"4. Borrowing Drills"},{"id":"s5","label":"5. Lifetime Challenges"},{"id":"s6","label":"6. Debugging Walkthroughs"},{"id":"s7","label":"7. Traits & Generics"},{"id":"s8","label":"8. Concurrency Solutions"},{"id":"s9","label":"9. Async Solutions"},{"id":"s10","label":"10. Mini Project Rubrics"},{"id":"summary","label":"Summary"},{"id":"faqs","label":"FAQ"},{"id":"glossary","label":"Glossary"},{"id":"references","label":"References"},{"id":"disclaimer","label":"Disclaimer"}],"related":[{"title":"Rust — Practice Questions","tag":"Programming","time":"21 min"},{"title":"Rust — Interview Questions","tag":"Programming","time":"35 min"},{"title":"Rust — Complete Tutorial","tag":"Programming","time":"41 min"}],"html":"<section id=\"objectives\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Learning Objectives</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Verify practice attempts with detailed reasoning.</li>\n          <li>Learn optimization and stylistic alternatives.</li>\n          <li>Self-grade with clear rubrics.</li>\n        </ul>\n        <div class=\"my-4 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-red-500/40 bg-red-500/10 text-red-900 dark:text-red-100 p-4\"><div class=\"flex items-start gap-3\"><div class=\"mt-0.5 shrink-0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-5 w-5\"><path d=\"m21.73 18-8-14a2 2 0 0 0-3.48 0l-8 14A2 2 0 0 0 4 21h16a2 2 0 0 0 1.73-3Z\"/><path d=\"M12 9v4\"/><path d=\"M12 17h.01\"/></svg></div><div class=\"min-w-0 flex-1\"><p class=\"text-sm font-semibold\">Discipline</p><div class=\"mt-1 text-sm\">Attempt every question in the workbook before opening this key.</div></div></div></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s1\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">1. MCQ Answers</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <A n={1}>(b) <code>let</code> — the default binding.</A>\n        <A n={2}>(b) reference count — the pointer is bumped, no new allocation.</A>\n        <A n={3}>(a) Send — <code>Sync</code> is for shared references.</A>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1451187580459-43490279c0fa?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 1 — Answer-key methodology: reason first, code second, alternatives third.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s2\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">2. Output Prediction</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <A n={10}>Prints \"hi\". <code>s</code> moved into <code>t</code>; using <code>s</code> after would fail.</A>\n        <A n={11}>Prints 4 — <code>push</code> mutates in place; length grows by 1.</A>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s3\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">3. Ownership Puzzles</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <A n={30}>\n          <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>let s = String::from(&quot;hi&quot;);\nlet t = s.clone(); // now both usable\nprintln!(&quot;{}, {}&quot;, s, t);</code></pre></div>\n          Prefer references over clones when perf matters.\n        </A>\n        <A n={31}>Return a tuple or a small struct — zero-cost.<div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>fn split(s: &amp;str) -&gt; (&amp;str, &amp;str) { s.split_at(1) }</code></pre></div></A>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s4\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">4. Borrowing Drills</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <A n={60}>Take <code>&amp;str</code> instead of <code>String</code>:<div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>fn hello(name: &amp;str) { println!(&quot;Hi, {name}&quot;); }</code></pre></div></A>\n        <A n={61}>Rust's aliasing-XOR-mutation rule prevents readers from seeing torn writes without needing locks.</A>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s5\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">5. Lifetime Challenges</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <A n={90}>\n          <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>fn longest&lt;&#x27;a&gt;(a: &amp;&#x27;a str, b: &amp;&#x27;a str) -&gt; &amp;&#x27;a str {\n    if a.len() &gt; b.len() { a } else { b }\n}</code></pre></div>\n          The output must not outlive either input.\n        </A>\n        <A n={91}><code>'static</code> for string literals, program-lifetime globals, or values you leak intentionally.</A>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s6\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">6. Debugging Walkthroughs</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <A n={120}>The <code>&amp;v</code> keeps a shared borrow alive while <code>v.push</code> demands a mutable borrow. Fix by ending the shared borrow first:<div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>let v = vec![1,2,3];\n{\n    let r = &amp;v;\n    println!(&quot;{:?}&quot;, r);\n}\nlet mut v = v; v.push(4);</code></pre></div></A>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s7\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">7. Traits &amp; Generics</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <A n={160}>\n          <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>use std::fmt;\nstruct Point { x: f64, y: f64 }\nimpl fmt::Display for Point {\n    fn fmt(&amp;self, f: &amp;mut fmt::Formatter&lt;&#x27;_&gt;) -&gt; fmt::Result {\n        write!(f, &quot;({}, {})&quot;, self.x, self.y)\n    }\n}</code></pre></div>\n        </A>\n        <A n={161}>\n          <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>fn max&lt;T: PartialOrd&gt;(a: T, b: T) -&gt; T { if a &gt; b { a } else { b } }</code></pre></div>\n        </A>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s8\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">8. Concurrency Solutions</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <A n={200}>\n          <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>use std::sync::{Arc, Mutex};\nuse std::thread;\nlet counter = Arc::new(Mutex::new(0));\nlet mut handles = vec![];\nfor _ in 0..4 {\n    let c = Arc::clone(&amp;counter);\n    handles.push(thread::spawn(move || { *c.lock().unwrap() += 1; }));\n}\nfor h in handles { h.join().unwrap(); }</code></pre></div>\n        </A>\n        <A n={201}>Use <code>mpsc::channel</code>; each worker sends 1; main sums receipts.</A>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544197150-b99a580bb7a8?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 2 — Choosing between Arc+Mutex and channels: shared state vs message passing.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s9\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">9. Async Solutions</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <A n={260}>\n          <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>let urls = vec![&quot;a&quot;, &quot;b&quot;, &quot;c&quot;];\nlet results = futures::future::join_all(\n    urls.iter().map(|u| reqwest::get(*u))\n).await;</code></pre></div>\n        </A>\n        <A n={261}><code>tokio::time::timeout(dur, fut).await</code> — returns <code>Err(Elapsed)</code> on expiry.</A>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s10\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">10. Mini Project Rubrics</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <table class=\"w-full border-collapse text-sm\">\n          <thead><tr class=\"border-b\"><th class=\"p-2 text-left\">Criterion</th><th class=\"p-2 text-left\">Weight</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\">Correctness</td><td class=\"p-2\">40%</td></tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\">Idiomatic Rust</td><td class=\"p-2\">20%</td></tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\">Error handling</td><td class=\"p-2\">15%</td></tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\">Tests</td><td class=\"p-2\">15%</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"p-2\">Documentation</td><td class=\"p-2\">10%</td></tr>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"summary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Summary &amp; Key Takeaways</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>The best answer isn't always the shortest — clarity + safety + performance is the winning trio.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"faqs\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">FAQ</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Multiple correct answers?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Often — the rubric rewards clarity and correctness over style.</div></details>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"glossary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Glossary</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li><strong>Rubric</strong> — grading criteria with weights.</li>\n          <li><strong>Idiomatic</strong> — matches community convention.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"references\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">References</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\"><References /></div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"disclaimer\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Disclaimer</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Solutions provided for study — multiple correct approaches exist.</p>\n      </div></section>"}